    - 'webpack-assets-manifest > deepmerge':
        reason: 'Checked 2026-11-05 on webpack-assets-manifest@6.5.5 > deepmerge@4.3.1 (also installed through its types package). Prototype replacement needs an attacker-controlled source object containing __proto__ passed to mergeObject(). The plugin imports deepmerge only in maybeMerge() when options.merge is enabled; webpack.config.js uses new WebpackAssetsManifest() with merge disabled by default. This is build tooling, outside applicant requests. No fixed deepmerge release exists. Remove when upstream drops or fixes deepmerge; reassess if manifest merging is enabled.'
